 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "This is a Flask-style framework (package `tessel`). The order is:\n\n1. `Tessel.__call__` (`src/tessel/app.py:1618`) just delegates to `wsgi_entry`.\n2. `Tessel.wsgi_entry` (`src/tessel/app.py:1566`) is the real WSGI entry. It runs steps 3 to 7 inside a try/finally.\n3. `Tessel.request_context(environ)` (`src/tessel/app.py:1501`) builds the context (`AppContext`, `src/tessel/ctx.py`) with the request object and URL adapter.\n4. `AppContext.push` (`src/tessel/ctx.py:416`) does the following:\n   - Binds the context to the context var and sends `appcontext_pushed`.\n   - Opens the session via `_get_session()`.\n   - Calls `match_request` (`src/tessel/ctx.py:405`), which routes the URL and stores `url_rule` and `view_args`, or a routing exception, on the request.\n5. `Tessel.run_full_request` (`src/tessel/app.py:992`) does the following:\n   - Sends `request_started`.\n   - Calls `preprocess_request` (`src/tessel/app.py:1366`), which runs the before-request functions. If one returns a value, the view is skipped.\n6. `Tessel.run_view` (`src/tessel/app.py`, just above line 976) does the following:\n   - Raises any stored routing exception.\n   - Short-circuits automatic OPTIONS requests.\n   - Otherwise calls `self.ensure_sync(self.view_functions[rule.endpoint])(**view_args)`, which is the view function (line 990).\n\nAfter the view returns, `finalize_request` (`src/tessel/app.py:1021`) turns the return value into a response through `make_response` and `finalize_reply`. Then `wsgi_entry` calls `response(environ, start_response)` and `ctx.pop(error)` for teardown.",
